#[doc = "# Product requirements\n\nOrigin: customer vision, 2026-11-07. Mealshop is a working name.\nThe [feature index](../page_specs_readme_md/index.html) maps F01–F23 one-to-one to acceptance contracts.\n\n## Cross-cutting requirements\n- N01: Rust/Axum/Tokio backend and Flutter client; standalone and free Nextcloud `ExApp` deployment.\n- N02: Selectable Git/file, PostgreSQL, SQLite or MariaDB persistence, with portable versioned data.\n- N03: Precise quantities, configurable presentation, reproducible nutrition and explicit unknowns.\n- N04: Household isolation, dietary exclusions above recommendations, consented calendar/learning use.\n- N05: AGPL-3.0-only complete software; paid official app, self-build allowed, free/paid hosted tiers.\n- N06: Imported recipes share their source URL only, including via collections, MCP and federation.\n- N07: Multi-day processes and reminders survive restart and explain delivery limitations.\n- N08: Spec-driven development, ADRs and CI with Renovate, builds, docs/Pages, audit, SBOM, metrics and MSRV.\n\n- N09: English is the coded/canonical base with stable language-independent IDs and separate translations. German/English i18n from the outset: UI, content names/search, exact locale-aware quantity input and number/date/plural formatting; preserve source language when translations are absent.\n- N10: Vue 3 product web clients for Nextcloud and standalone hosting. The existing framework-free web surface is a pragmatic demo only; significant UX/UI work belongs in the product workflow.\n\n## Scope and unresolved decisions\nM0 delivered the bootstrap. F02 adds a read-only, versioned nutrition starter catalogue and\nstateless demo accepted in PR #4. Its USDA snapshots are CC0; long-term provider coverage/refresh, identity/authentication,\ncalendar provider, database migration/sync details, payment provider, attestation feasibility,\nnotification transport, federation protocol and concrete paid tiers remain open. No customer\nprice, health guarantee or provider commitment is inferred from the vision.\n\n## Traceability\nN01 → F01/F18; N02 → F18; N03 → F02/F03/F04; N04 → F09/F10/F11;\nN05 → F19; N06 → F05/F16/F17/F20; N07 → F12/F13/F14; N08 → F01.\nEach feature plan must link its tests to its numbered acceptance criteria before Done.\n\nN09 → F21 (all client features); N10 → F22/F18. F02 is Done following customer merge of PR #4.\n\nF23 expands the kitchen reference catalogue from the customer ingredient list with exact BLS/USDA\nsource mappings; unresolved product profiles remain explicitly unknown.\n\nF23 is accepted through PR #5. F04/F18 now starts local recipe authoring and immutable file\nrevisions with pinned nutrition inputs; authenticated ownership, scaling and other adapters\nremain future work. See [recipe guide](../page_docs_guides_recipes_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_docs_requirements_md {}

#[doc = "# Roadmap\n\nThis is a proposed delivery order, not a promise of dates. Dependencies can change after review.\n\n| Milestone | Outcome | Features |\n|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Runnable server, specs, docs and delivery pipeline | F01 |\n| M1 | Recipe/nutrition foundation, household constraints, first storage/deployment slice, localization and product web clients | F02–F04, F09, F18, F21–F23 |\n| M2 | Shared recipes, family plans, shopping, guided cooking, incremental preference feedback | F05–F07, F10–F12 |\n| M3 | Barcode, long dough processes, inventory/offers, imports, MCP | F08, F13, F15–F17 |\n| M4 | Brewing/fermentation and commercial operations | F14, F19 |\n| M5 | Opt-in federation | F20 |\n\nM1 starts with local recipe revision files and pinned BLS/USDA nutrition sources.\nThe authenticated identity model, Git/SQL adapters and Flutter interaction remain to be specified. F18 spans several milestones: a first backend\nis not completion of the four-backend/Nextcloud/client acceptance contract. Online learning\nstarts with inspectable rules and feedback; production ML follows measured benefit.\n\nPR #4 is accepted. Its browser surface is a demo only. F21 starts with pragmatic demo localization;\nF22 specifies Vue 3 shells for Nextcloud and standalone hosting before product UI implementation.\n\nPR #5 is accepted (F23 Done; initial F21 slice accepted). F04/F18 now starts local recipe\nauthoring and file persistence; proportional scaling and production integrations remain open.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_roadmap_md {}

#[doc = "# Technical debt and validation backlog\n\n- F04/F18 starts bounded local recipe file persistence. Auth, rate limiting, Git/SQL adapters,\n  product-client integration remain open. No shared/hosted access is implemented.\n- Validate actual Nextcloud `AppAPI` support and Flutter offline/notification behaviour (F18/F12).\n- F02 originally supplied frozen CC0 USDA oats/chia values. F23 adds the curated BLS/USDA kitchen catalogue.\n  Broader coverage, provider refresh, density, cooking yield/retention and component measurements\n  remain future work (F02/F03); psyllium composition is deliberately unknown.\n- Validate official-app service admission without weakening AGPL rights (F19 / ADR 0004).\n- Binary-size metrics initially have no previous baseline. No performance budget is invented.\n\nThese are explicit future work, not completed features or ignored CI findings.\n\n- F23 catalogue generation is offline; 29 identities still lack exact composition. The current\n  file is near the pre-existing 1 MiB demo loader bound; wider loading belongs with F18.\n- BLS available carbohydrate and food folate stay separate from other definitions; complete\n  product coverage and additional micronutrients need reviewed mappings, never inferred conversion.\n- F21 first slice covers de/en demo messages, names and decimals. Reviewed source/evidence prose\n  translations, date/plural/error parameters across all clients and production locale negotiation remain open.\n\n- Recipe file storage is a Linux/local-filesystem slice with an exclusive lock, manual crash\n  recovery and 1000-revision capacity. POST idempotency and non-Unix crash durability remain open.\n\n- Lowest-priority deferred item (customer request): cross-device preference synchronization.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_technical_debt_md {}

