#[doc = "# Decisions for ingredient catalogue and nutrition\n\n- [ADR 0002](../page_docs_adr_0002_quantities_and_nutrition_md/index.html): preserve quantity dimensions,\n  provenance and unknowns; perform no implicit volume/mass conversions.\n\n## Feature-local decisions\n2026-11-07 (Proposal, reversible within this slice):\n- Use bounded scaled integers (six decimal places) and checked rational arithmetic through\n  final display rounding. JSON amounts are strings; original decimal spelling is retained.\n  `serde`/`serde_json` (MIT OR Apache-2.0) provide typed API\n  serialization already present transitively; declare them directly now that they are used.\n- Retain a fixed per-100-g edible-portion basis and a named nutrient registry with explicit\n  units; serving counts are positive integers. F03 will extend user-facing quantity units.\n- Read a validated immutable catalogue at startup, using bundled public-domain/CC0 USDA SR\n  Legacy snapshots by default. An optional local JSON file replaces the whole catalogue.\n  This does not decide the persistent household storage architecture of F18.\n- A stateless estimate endpoint takes ingredient IDs/grams/servings/context and returns\n  complete or explicitly partial totals, retained provenance and preparation warnings.\n- Supply a minimal same-origin browser workbench instead of starting the full Flutter shell.\n  Only public operator-provided catalogue records are readable; no user data is persisted.\n- Reviewed educational notes carry source, applicability and limitations separately from\n  measured composition. No dose/benefit is inferred when component data is absent.\n\nProvider curation/refresh, a complete nutrient vocabulary and general cooking-retention models\nremain future refinements. The starter catalogue is deliberately small, not an authoritative\nfood/allergen database. Customer authorization to start F02 is not acceptance of a finished PR.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_adrs_md {}

#[doc = "# Plan for ingredient catalogue and nutrition\n\n## Affected modules\n`src/quantities.rs`: validated decimal amounts and gram quantities.\n`src/nutrition/`: catalogue model/validation and pure nutrient calculation.\n`src/api.rs`, `src/lib.rs`, `src/main.rs`: read-only catalogue and stateless calculation HTTP API.\n`src/web/`: browser workbench. `data/`: reviewed catalogue and original source snapshots.\n`tests/`: acceptance checks and fixtures. No new crate or storage abstraction.\n\n## Tasks\n- [x] Refine acceptance/UX notes and record implementation proposals before implementation.\n- [x] Define failing acceptance tests for provenance, scaling, missing data and education (AC 1–4, 5–9).\n- [x] Implement typed decimal quantities, validated catalogue, pure aggregation and rounding (AC 1–3, 6–9).\n- [x] Freeze and verify primary-source starter records and evidence notes (AC 1, 4).\n- [x] Expose read-only/search/detail API, stateless calculations and startup catalogue loading (AC 5–9).\n- [x] Build and exercise the browser workbench including errors/unknowns (AC 3, 10).\n- [x] Run quality/security/MSRV checks and prepare the reviewable feature branch/demo.\n\n## Validation\nDerive black-box HTTP tests from this specification before implementing the handlers. Check\nsource-record preservation, known arithmetic/portion scaling, exact decimal behaviour and\nrounding boundaries; distinguish partial/unknown from zero; reject invalid/oversized input.\nVerify the bundled values directly against the frozen USDA source records, not copied assertions.\nExercise custom-catalogue startup validation and existing health/startup regression tests.\nBrowser-check normal, unknown/partial, error and narrow-screen flows. Run the repository gate,\nMSRV and CI; record exact outcomes before marking implementation review-ready.\n\n## Evidence\nSee [validation.md](../page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_validation_md/index.html) and [the demo guide](../page_docs_guides_nutrition_md/index.html).\n\n## Acceptance\n- [x] Customer merged [PR #4](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/pull/4) and confirmed acceptance (2026-11-07).\n"]
