pub mod page_specs_0009_household_profiles_adrs_md {}

#[doc = "# F09 local household slice\n\n- [x] Separate local operator access and protected profile storage (AC 1, 4).\n- [x] Record allergy/intolerance notes, hard exclusions and soft dislikes separately (AC 1).\n- [x] Group review unions constraints, resolves known aliases and preserves unknowns (AC 2–3).\n- [x] Revision-aware correction, authorized JSON export and member removal (AC 4).\n- [x] Add pragmatic keyed de/en demo flow and operator/recovery documentation.\n- [x] Complete repository gate and review PR; full F09 completion requested by customer.\n\nTests in tests/household.rs cover unauthorized reads/writes, conflicts, aliases, hard/soft\nseparation, unknowns, restart/export/removal, invalid data and interrupted/corrupt storage.\nFull allergen mapping and hosted identity integration remain future work; unblocked candidates\nalways require review. No learning component exists that can relax a hard constraint.\n\nValidation: 35 Rust tests, six locale tests, catalogue and conversion verifiers, fmt/clippy,\nlicenses, audit, strict rustdoc and MSRV 1.85 passed locally. Browser confirmed unauthorized\naccess rejection, authorized profile save and hard-exclusion blocking.\n\n## Complete F09 acceptance\n- [x] Structured hard allergen IDs and separate intolerance/free-text notes; backwards-compatible profile loading (AC 1).\n- [x] Positive source-backed food classifications, exact identity/state filtering, group hard matches with provenance (AC 2–3).\n- [x] Operator/read-only permission separation, including write/delete denial and authorized export (AC 1, 4).\n- [x] Existing correction/removal, unknown-data and restart/failure acceptance tests retained (AC 3–4).\n- [x] Final local gate; current-commit CI evidence is recorded in PR #12.\n\nHosted accounts are not part of this local feature contract. Source coverage remains positive-only\nand incremental; incomplete coverage always requires review, never an inferred safe result.\n\nFinal acceptance results: [validation](../page_specs_0009_household_profiles_validation_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0009_household_profiles_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Household members and dietary constraints\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M1\n\n## User value\nPlan meals safely for everyone eating.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given a household member, intolerances/allergies and disliked ingredients are recorded separately with explicit access controls.\n2. Given a group meal, hard exclusions cover all attendees and known ingredient aliases; a dislike is a soft preference.\n3. Given missing ingredient or allergen data, a candidate is flagged for review rather than declared safe.\n4. Given member data, authorized people can correct, export and delete it; learning never relaxes a hard exclusion.\n\n## Out of scope\nDiagnosis or guaranteed absence of cross-contamination.\n\n## UX notes\nSee ux-notes.md.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F09](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0009_household_profiles_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0009_household_profiles_adrs_md/index.html).\n\n## Completion scope\nProtected local single-household profiles with operator and optional read-only credentials,\nrevision-aware correction/export/removal, structured hard allergen groups, separate intolerance\nand allergy notes, explicit ingredient exclusions and soft dislikes. Positive food-identity\nclassifications apply only to matching catalogue records/states. Group evaluation unions all\nattendees' hard constraints and known ingredient aliases. Unknown or incomplete allergen data\nalways requires review; no result establishes cross-contamination safety. Learning has no\nwrite path to profiles. Hosted accounts/roles remain a separate deployment feature.\n\nCompleted evidence is recorded in validation.md. Data coverage can grow independently of this\nfeature; absent classifications never mean allergen absence.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0009_household_profiles_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Household demo UX\n\nThe existing demo adds a protected household section with session-only token input, load,\nmember selection/new member, name, allergy/intolerance notes, hard exclusions and soft dislikes.\nIngredient selections use canonical IDs and localized catalogue names. Save/remove require\noperator authorization; conflicts retain edits and explain reload/reconciliation. Load/export\nis explicit. Evaluation reviews current recipe ingredients for all recorded members and\nshows blocked or review-required, never safe. Tokens/profiles are never stored in browser\nstorage. Empty/new and access/error states use English-base keyed de/en messages.\n\nStructured allergen groups are separately selectable and always hard constraints. Additional\nintolerance notes remain separate and require review. Readers can load/export/evaluate; save\nand removal require operator rights and cannot be enabled by a UI role claim.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0009_household_profiles_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F09 completion evidence\n\nStatus: Done for the local household contract; customer requested completion in PR #12.\n\n## Acceptance mapping\n- AC 1: separate structured hard allergen IDs, allergy notes, intolerance notes, hard ingredient\n  exclusions and dislikes. Operator/read-only credentials enforce all API access; unknown\n  credentials are denied and readers cannot edit/remove. Legacy profiles load new fields empty.\n- AC 2: selected attendees' exclusions and positive allergen matches are unioned. Known names\n  and aliases resolve conservatively. Dislikes never remove exclusions. Matches retain member,\n  ingredient, group, source and reference version. No learning writer exists for profiles.\n- AC 3: unknown ingredients, unstructured notes, incomplete positive-only allergen coverage and\n  cross-contact never yield a safe result. Unblocked results always require review. Reference\n  classifications apply only to matching catalogue source record IDs and states.\n- AC 4: authorized correction, revision conflicts, JSON export, removal and restart are tested.\n  Reader write/delete attempts fail; interrupted/corrupt storage fails closed without replacing\n  good state. Backups/exports are outside subsequent server deletion, as documented.\n\n## Automated evidence\n36 tests passed with `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`. Household acceptance tests\ncover existing access/restart/removal cases plus structured milk/soy constraints for multiple\nattendees, milk identity in lactose-free milk, read-only profile export/evaluation, denied\nwrites/deletion, unknown members/data and structured-field persistence. Six locale tests pass.\nCatalogue/import/conversion checks and `scripts/verify_allergens.py` pass (106 positive\nidentity classifications, 14 groups). Fmt, clippy, licenses, audit, strict rustdoc and MSRV\n1.85 pass. Current-commit CI links are recorded in PR #12.\n\n## Browser evidence\nAn operator created a demo member with the milk allergen group. Evaluating milk in the\ncurrent ingredients returned blocked. Loading profiles with the separate reader credential\nworked, while attempting to save changes was rejected and inputs remained available.\n\n## Bounds\nDone applies to local household profiles and dietary review, not hosted account management,\nmedical diagnosis, universal allergen coverage or guaranteed absence of cross-contact.\nData coverage can grow independently without relaxing hard constraints or unknown handling.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0009_household_profiles_validation_md {}

#[doc = "# Decisions for Family meal planning and calendar attendance\n\n- [ADR 0003](../page_docs_adr_0003_persistence_and_data_boundaries_md/index.html)\n- [ADR 0005](../page_docs_adr_0005_privacy_and_learning_md/index.html)\n- [ADR 0006](../page_docs_adr_0006_durable_process_schedules_md/index.html)\n\n## Feature-local decisions\n2026-11-07: Acceptance criteria capture the customer vision; unspecified implementation choices remain proposals. No future feature is implemented by this bootstrap.\n\n- [ADR 0011: family plans](../page_docs_adr_0011_family_meal_planning_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0010_meal_planning_adrs_md {}

#[doc = "# F10 family planning acceptance\n\n- [x] Protected persisted date/meal slots with pinned recipe revisions, attendees and servings (AC 1).\n- [x] Manual selection and constraint-compatible reviewed suggestions with rejected reasons (AC 1, 5).\n- [x] Consented read-only calendar snapshot import, visible source and manual override (AC 2).\n- [x] Active/elapsed/advance estimates and explicit unknown/batch-size timing uncertainty (AC 3).\n- [x] Preview/apply replacement/removal with scaled nutrition and shopping requirement deltas (AC 4).\n- [x] Profile/plan revision conflicts, renewed review markers, source revision retention (AC 4–5).\n- [x] Acceptance tests for constraints, consent, overrides, time, conflicts, restart and failures.\n- [x] Browser acceptance and full local repository gate; current-commit CI evidence in the PR.\n\nTests in tests/planning.rs map directly to the five acceptance criteria. Current local scope,\ncalendar import format and the distinction from live providers/F06 are documented in the guide\nand ADR 0011. Source uncertainty is retained; unknown data never becomes safe automatically.\n\nStatus: Done for the documented local/import-based F10 contract after local and browser acceptance.\nSee [validation](../page_specs_0010_meal_planning_validation_md/index.html). No live provider or F06 shopping execution is implied.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0010_meal_planning_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Family meal planning and calendar attendance\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M2\n\n## User value\nChoose feasible meals for the family and adapt when plans change.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given a day/meal and attendees, a planner can select recipes manually or request constraint-compatible suggestions.\n2. Given consented calendar access, attendance is proposed with a visible source and can be overridden without editing the external calendar.\n3. Given per-day preparation windows, suggestions distinguish active work, total elapsed time and advance preparation.\n4. Given a last-minute attendance/time change, the user can choose an alternative, rescale servings and preview shopping-list changes before applying them.\n5. Given no feasible meal, the planner explains the conflicting constraints instead of silently violating intolerances.\n\n## Out of scope\nAutonomous calendar writes or purchases.\n\n## UX notes\nSee ux-notes.md.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F10](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0010_meal_planning_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0010_meal_planning_adrs_md/index.html).\n\n## Implementation contract\nLocal protected planning uses F09 operator/reader roles and immutable recipe revisions. Calendar\nattendance is supplied through a consented read-only snapshot import with source/date/event and\nmapped household IDs; no specific live provider is implied. Preparation is estimated from ordered\nrecipe steps; scaled batch-time uncertainty is shown for review. Preview/apply revisions prevent\nstale profile/plan decisions, and known hard/time conflicts cannot be acknowledged away.\nShopping changes are plan-derived mass requirements, not completion of F06 purchase workflows.\nUnknown allergen data remains review-required. Hosted provider adapters and process scheduling\nbelong to their own features; F10 does not autonomously write external calendars or make purchases.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0010_meal_planning_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Pragmatic family-planning demo\n\nUse household credentials already present in the demo. Load family/plans explicitly; choose\nparticipants, date/meal, pinned recipe and preparation budgets. Both manual selection and a\nbounded multi-select candidate list support suggestions. Show blocked reasons, current profile\nnotes, timing uncertainty, source/attendance overrides, scaled nutrition and shopping deltas.\nA separate review checkbox and Apply action commit a feasible preview; changed fields invalidate\nit. Read-only users can preview but server authorization rejects mutation. Errors keep inputs.\nSaved slots can be loaded, replaced or removed after an explicit removal preview.\n\nCalendar input is a bounded JSON attendance snapshot, with source/date/event/proposed member IDs.\nConsent is separate from import and manual attendance override is explicit. No external writes.\nUnknown timing/data yields conflicts or dietary review, never an inferred safe result. Strings\nuse English-base keyed resources with German equivalents; this remains a disposable demo.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0010_meal_planning_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F10 acceptance evidence\n\nStatus: Done for the documented local family-planning and read-only attendance-import contract.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Protected manual recipe selection and bounded suggestions use pinned revisions, selected\n   attendees and F09 review. Known hard exclusions reject candidates; dislikes only rank them.\n2. Consented calendar snapshots retain source/event/date/proposal. Tests verify missing consent\n   rejection, source display and explicit manual attendance override without any external write.\n   The actual supported adapter is JSON snapshot import, not a live provider connection.\n3. Step timing distinguishes active, sequential elapsed and advance lead. Tests cover insufficient\n   active/elapsed windows and unknown step timing. UI makes original-batch timing uncertainty\n   explicit when portions change; no inferred parallelism or batch-time multiplier is claimed.\n4. Preview/apply supports alternatives, changed attendees/servings and removals. Tests verify\n   signed grocery deltas, derived persisted shopping requirements, revision conflict rejection,\n   explicit dietary acknowledgement, pinned historical recipe inputs and restart round trips.\n5. Suggestions return rejected conflict reasons and no-feasible explanations; both API and\n   browser tests verify hard constraints cannot be bypassed by acknowledgement or soft dislikes.\n\n## Automated results\n`cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`: 40 tests passed, none skipped, including four family\nplanning journeys. Additional focused planning/household runs passed after final arithmetic\nerror handling cleanup. Six Node locale tests and JS syntax checks passed. Catalogue import,\nnutrition source, conversion and allergen verifiers passed. Rustfmt, clippy with warnings denied,\nrelease build, licenses, cargo-audit, strict rustdoc and MSRV 1.85.0 passed. Current-commit CI\nlinks and outcomes are recorded in the PR.\n\nStorage tests simulate interrupted and corrupt plan snapshots; startup fails closed and releases\nlocks on failure. Reads/export remain protected; readers cannot apply. Existing F09 access,\nprofile export/removal/conflict/restart and F03/F04 nutrition/quantity tests remain green.\n\n## Browser results\nWith fictional profiles (one milk exclusion) and oat/milk recipes, suggestions retained the oat\nrecipe and rejected milk. The preview showed current member notes, active 600 s / elapsed\n2400 s / advance 1200 s and +200 g oats for four servings. Explicit acknowledgement/apply saved\nrevision 1 and 200 g derived demand; reloading preserved the pinned meal. Setting available\nactive time to zero produced no feasible meal and distinct timing/dietary conflict explanations.\n\n## Scope and limitations\nCalendar access is a user-consented, read-only attendance snapshot import with already mapped\nhousehold IDs. Live polling, OAuth, ICS recurrence/timezone expansion, external calendar writes,\npurchases, inventory and F06's full shopping workflow remain separate work. Review never\nestablishes allergen safety; data gaps, cross-contact and batch-time changes remain explicit.\nCapacity: 100 meal slots / 1 MiB local snapshot and 50 candidate revisions per suggestion call.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0010_meal_planning_validation_md {}

