#[doc = "# Vue 3 product web clients\n\nStatus: In progress\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer (after PR #4 merge, 2026-11-07)\nMilestone: M1\n\n## User value\nUse a proper web application inside Nextcloud or on a standalone Mealshop server.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. The Nextcloud client uses Vue 3 and compatible Nextcloud components, respects host\n   navigation/theme/accessibility, and loads assets/API calls correctly through `AppAPI`/proxy paths.\n2. The standalone server client uses Vue 3 with its own navigation/authentication shell and\n   connects to the same domain APIs. Shared code boundaries are chosen from real common needs.\n3. Both clients use F21 language/content/number contracts from the outset; domain calculations\n   stay on the Rust/API side and are not copied from the disposable demo.\n4. Supported Nextcloud/`AppAPI`/Vue component versions, authentication, CSRF/CSP, base paths and\n   deployment packaging are verified against actual installations before claiming compatibility.\n5. The existing framework-free nutrition demo is explicitly a temporary test surface. Extending\n   it does not establish product UX or replace either client. Design effort stays minimal there.\n6. Product UX is specified/reviewed before implementation. If significant design work is needed,\n   coordinate a dedicated UX/UI agent with the customer instead of expanding the demo design.\n\n## Authorized implementation (2026-11-09)\nCustomer requests a native Nextcloud 35 application with complete existing backend workflows,\nnot an isolated reference page; shared households with explicit invitations and roles were chosen.\nBuild integration/authentication/storage boundaries before domain screens. See ux-notes.md and\nADR 0012. No placeholders for planned features; a later pass is visual refinement only.\n\n## Out of scope\nStandalone shell and Flutter are separate deliverables. Unimplemented product-vision features\nare not implied by exposing the existing domain APIs.\n\n## UX notes\nSee [ux-notes.md](../page_specs_0022_product_web_clients_ux_notes_md/index.html); native Nextcloud hierarchy is customer-mandated.\n\n## Links\n[ADR 0007](../page_docs_adr_0007_localization_and_web_clients_md/index.html),\n[F21](../page_specs_0021_internationalization_specification_md/index.html), [F18](../page_specs_0018_storage_deployment_specification_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0022_product_web_clients_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Nextcloud product experience\n\nStatus: Ready for implementation, customer authorized 2026-11-09.\n\n## Design contract\nNextcloud owns the header, navigation chrome, typography, theme and focus conventions.\nUse `@nextcloud/vue` 9 (Vue 3), Composition API and strict `TypeScript`. No global reset,\nweb fonts, decorative cards, hero layouts, gradients or alternative component system.\nTaste contributes alignment, rhythm and screenshot review only: its website generators,\nhero/motion requirements and marketing gates conflict with the customer's native-app brief.\nUI UX Pro Max contributes search, progressive disclosure, keyboard/focus and error recovery.\nAwesome Design was not found in the installed skill directories; no capability is assumed.\n\n## Information architecture\n- Household context first: create a household or accept an addressed invitation.\n- Recipes: list, create, read, revise and exact serving preview using existing domain APIs.\n- Meal plan: attendance, recipe revisions, time constraints, suggestions, review, shopping preview,\n  apply and removal. Calendar snapshots require explicit consent; no live calendar is implied.\n- Ingredients: searchable catalogue, translated identity, exact nutrient values, provenance,\n  original-language fallback and explicit unknowns.\n- Household: dietary profiles and membership are distinct sections. Hard exclusions and soft\n  dislikes never share a control. Health-data visibility is explained before accepting access.\n\n## Membership contract\nCustomer chose shared households with invitations and read/write roles. Proposed concrete\nroles: owner manages membership, editor modifies domain data, reader reads/exports and reviews.\nInvitations target an exact Nextcloud user ID and require explicit acceptance. No automatic\ninstance-wide household. Server checks current membership on every request. Unknown account\nnames do not expose the Nextcloud directory. Owner cannot be removed without transferring ownership.\n\n## Interaction contract\nOne page title and clear primary action. Native navigation, dialogs, fields, notices and empty\nstates. Persistent labels, inline errors, retained input on failure, conflict recovery without\nsilent overwrite. Loading and retry paths on every remote screen; no fake success or demo data.\nLists lead to URL-addressable detail pages. Back returns to the list and keeps its search.\nAt narrow widths navigation collapses using native components, forms stack, details wrap and\nnutrient tables retain readable headers. Native theme variables only; inherited reduced motion.\nKeyboard focus moves to the new page heading; dialog focus trapping belongs to `NcDialog`.\n\n## Verification\nReal host: customer-provided Nextcloud 35.0.2 / `AppAPI` 35.0.0 at loopback port 8080.\nVerify session/CSRF, proxy paths, refresh/deep links, two users, reader denial, invitation/revocation,\nrevision conflicts, unknown nutrition, light/dark, 320/768/1024/1440 widths and axe checks.\nA second visual pass may refine spacing and copy, but cannot stand in for missing workflows.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0022_product_web_clients_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# Nextcloud client validation\n\nEnvironment: local Nextcloud 35.0.2, `AppAPI` 35.0.0, Chromium, native embedded route. Only fictional browser-test households and profiles were used. Host data was not reset.\n\n## Completed checks\n\n- Catalogue import check and offline verifier: 313 records; source identity and unknown composition preserved.\n- `node --test tests/i18n.test.mjs`: passed.\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`: passed.\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`: passed after correcting generated documentation formatting.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`: 43 passed, zero skipped.\n- `cargo deny check licenses`: passed with explicit version-scoped dependency exceptions.\n- `cargo audit`: passed, 140 locked dependencies checked.\n- Client `npm run format:check`: passed.\n- Client `npm test`: four tests passed.\n- Client `npm run build`: strict type checking and production build passed; 620.70 kB JavaScript, 80.26 kB CSS before compression.\n- Client `npm audit --audit-level=moderate`: zero vulnerabilities.\n- Final `docker build -t mealshop.local/mealshop:0.1.0 .` passed (image da02292bdfa1). `python3 scripts/test_exapp_container.py` passed for rootless TCP and Unix sockets, lifecycle authentication, assets, custom CSRF header, JSON content type and private persistence.\n\n## Browser evidence and limits\n\nThe Playwright suite drives household creation, addressed invitations, reader permissions, revocation, stale revision recovery, exact quantity display/scaling, original quantities, curated portions, dietary constraints, profile editing, planning and shopping-list application. It checks actual host light/dark themes, reduced motion, keyboard navigation, responsive bounds at 320–1440 pixels and automated accessibility rules. Screenshots and failure traces are private ignored local artifacts; accessibility automation does not establish complete WCAG conformance.\n\nFinal sequential run: `playwright test --config clients/nextcloud/playwright.config.ts` passed all four browser tests in 52.8 seconds. An earlier run during a simultaneous frontend rebuild timed out; the final run used stable assets.\n\n## Verified test-container deployment\n\nOn 2026-11-09, the customer explicitly approved the internal `nextcloud` trusted domain and container switch. The hostname was added at index 3 without replacing existing entries. The manual process was gracefully stopped, its storage lock released, and the prepared container started with the same secret, port and persistent directory. The container healthcheck passed.\n\nThe complete four-test Playwright suite passed against the container in 58.5 seconds. A subsequent graceful container restart preserved byte-equivalent canonical JSON responses for the authenticated owner's household list, memberships/roles, recipes, profiles and plans across all 14 test households. Startup restored enabled state and authenticated access without a manual enable hook. No private payload was printed.\n\nAll ten checks for the initial PR commit passed in GitHub CI, including image build, native client, Rust quality/coverage, MSRV, both build profiles, licences, advisories, SBOM and binary metrics. Deployment evidence updates receive the same CI checks.\n\nThe standalone shell, full production `HaRP` tunnel deployment and Nextcloud account deletion/recreation reconciliation are outside this completed native-client implementation and must not be presented as implemented. See the deployment guide and ADR 0012.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0022_product_web_clients_validation_md {}

#[doc = "# Decisions for the kitchen catalogue\n\n- [ADR 0008](../page_docs_adr_0008_curated_ingredient_sources_md/index.html): exact source matching, licensing,\n  English base/translations and distinct nutrient definitions.\n- [ADR 0002](../page_docs_adr_0002_quantities_and_nutrition_md/index.html): exact quantities and unknowns.\n- [ADR 0007](../page_docs_adr_0007_localization_and_web_clients_md/index.html): pragmatic demo, keyed i18n and Vue 3 product direction.\n"]
