#[doc = "# Plan for the kitchen catalogue\n\n- [x] Curate requested food identities/variants and classify exact source versus identity-only (AC 2–4).\n- [x] Extract primary BLS/USDA source selections with immutable source hashes/references (AC 3, 6).\n- [x] Implement deterministic import and independent provenance/unit/value verification (AC 3–6).\n- [x] Add English-base/translations model, multilingual search and exact demo locale presentation (AC 1, 7).\n- [x] Add separate available-carbohydrate/food-folate IDs and mixed-definition warnings (AC 5).\n- [x] Complete focused tests, browser exercise and repository quality gate; prepare review PR.\n- [x] Customer review/acceptance: PR #5 merged.\n\n## Validation\nSource verifier checks every mapped value against frozen primary data within the documented\nsix-decimal import tolerance, checks units and exact record identities, and rejects unsourced\nnumeric values. API tests cover exact flour/dairy/protein variants, unknown product profiles,\ntranslation identity/fallback, multilingual search and split carbohydrate definitions.\nLocale tests cover resource IDs/placeholders, regional fallbacks, exact big-number display and\ncomma/point input. Reuse F02 arithmetic/provenance regressions. Record results at delivery.\n\nResults: [delivery validation](../page_specs_0023_kitchen_ingredient_catalogue_validation_md/index.html). Customer accepted via PR #5.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0023_kitchen_ingredient_catalogue_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# English-base kitchen ingredient catalogue\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer (2026-11-07)\nMilestone: M1\n\n## User value\nTry real recipes with a broad set of familiar ingredients instead of a three-item catalogue.\nAll coded names/content have an English base and stable identifiers, with German translations\nkept separately. The existing browser surface remains a pragmatic demo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Canonical ingredient IDs, category identifiers and base names are language independent or\n   English. German names/aliases/forms live in keyed translation fields. Selecting a language\n   never rewrites identities, nutrients, units or canonical decimal strings.\n2. Include wheat/rye/spelt grain, their common German flour types and wholemeal forms, semolina,\n   water, skimmed/low-fat/whole/UHT/lactose-free milk, plant drinks, cocoa/sugar/xylitol/erythritol,\n   quark grades including double-cream identity, cream/butter/margarine/eggs, tofu/legumes/edamame/\n   quinoa, the requested vegetables, herbs, potatoes/skyr, conventional/wholemeal/legume pasta,\n   tomato products, protein powders/products, rice paper, beetroot, chicken cuts and varied cheeses.\n   Useful related seeds/nuts/oils/baking basics are included. Names distinguish raw/cooked,\n   fresh/dried, fortified/unfortified, product-specific and fat-in-dry-matter variants.\n3. Every numeric profile maps to an exact frozen primary source record with unit/basis, publisher,\n   version, retrieval date, licence and source uncertainty/acquisition metadata. Reviewed BLS 4.0\n   records provide German flour types and dairy variants; USDA adds appropriate herbs/reference powders.\n4. No nearest-food substitution: unresolved product variants are present as clearly named\n   identity-only records with unknown composition. Lentil flour is not lentil pasta; whey powder\n   is not a universal whey isolate; double-cream quark does not inherit 50%-in-dry-matter quark data.\n5. Keep BLS available carbohydrate separate from USDA by-difference carbohydrate, and food folate\n   separate from total folate/DFE. Mixed definitions yield separate/partial totals with an\n   explanatory warning, never a silent conversion. Existing oats/chia recipe results remain unchanged.\n6. Source extraction/import is reproducible offline from committed snapshots/selections. Preserve\n   original source cells/tokens and references; document six-decimal import normalization and\n   never convert unavailable/below-resolution positive data into claimed zero.\n7. Search finds English/German names and aliases, common plurals and multiword queries (e.g.\n   Weizen 405, Hafermilch, Magerquark, Kichererbsen, Eier). The demo uses keyed English-base UI\n   messages with German display and exact comma input/output, without product UI design expansion.\n\n## Current delivery scope\n313 identities: 284 source-backed profiles, 29 identity-only records; 3,778 mapped nutrient values\nacross 17 supported nutrient definitions. Data selections are in `data/catalogue-selection.json`.\nSource-backed means source composition exists, not that all 17 definitions are available or\nthat the food is a measured match for the customer's specific product.\n\n## Out of scope\nEvery worldwide brand, automatic provider refresh, invented product averages, exhaustive\nmicronutrient coverage, medical outcomes, storage adapters or production web clients.\nProduct-specific pulse pasta/protein products and other unresolved variants need verified\npackage/manufacturer records before their nutrients can be populated.\n\n## UX notes\nUse the existing demo and F21 language controls. Original source/evidence prose is labelled\nas original when no reviewed translation exists. No design system or Vue migration in this slice.\n\n## Links\n[F02](../page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_specification_md/index.html), [F21](../page_specs_0021_internationalization_specification_md/index.html),\n[F22](../page_specs_0022_product_web_clients_specification_md/index.html), [ADRs](../page_specs_0023_kitchen_ingredient_catalogue_adrs_md/index.html), [plan](../page_specs_0023_kitchen_ingredient_catalogue_plan_md/index.html).\n\nCustomer accepted this slice by merging PR #5.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0023_kitchen_ingredient_catalogue_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Delivery validation\n\nDate: 2026-11-07. Scope: F21 demo slice and F23 curated catalogue; acceptance pending.\n\n## Automated checks\nAll checks passed locally:\n- `python3 scripts/generate_docs.py --check`\n- `python3 scripts/import_catalogue.py --check`: 313 identities, 1,026,680 bytes.\n- `python3 scripts/verify_catalogue.py`: 284 source profiles, 29 identity-only records,\n  3,778 mapped numeric values independently compared with frozen primary records.\n- `node --check src/web/demo.mjs` and `node tests/i18n.test.mjs`: six locale tests passed.\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`: 19 tests passed, none skipped.\n- `cargo build --release --locked`\n- `cargo deny check licenses`\n- `cargo audit`: no vulnerabilities reported for the 54-dependency lockfile.\n- `RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --locked`\n- `cargo msrv verify -- cargo check --all-targets --locked`: Rust 1.85.0 compatible.\n\n## Browser exercise\nThe existing demo loaded 313 ingredients and 17 nutrient definitions. Switching English to\nGerman changed keyed messages and ingredient names. Entering 100,5 g oats and 25 g chia for\ntwo servings produced 256,22 kcal and 10,55 g protein per serving. Switching to English\npreserved the quantities and displayed 100.5 and 256.22. Invalid German `1.000` remained\ninvalid after switching to English and could not be calculated until explicitly edited.\nGerman search `Weizen 405` returned the exact wheat flour Type 405 record with BLS identity\nC214100 and CC-BY-4.0 attribution. Combining it with 1.5%-fat milk displayed available\ncarbohydrate separately. Reloading retained the selected language. At a 390 × 844 viewport,\nmeasured document scroll width equalled client width (375 px), without horizontal overflow.\n\n## Limits and review\nSource profiles are reference composition, not complete 17-nutrient profiles or measured\nmatches for every retail product. The 29 identity-only records deliberately contain no\ninvented values; manufacturer/package sources are future curation. BLS and USDA carbohydrate\nand folate definitions stay separate. The catalogue is close to the existing 1 MiB loading\nlimit; further substantial growth needs the F18 loading/storage slice. No limit was raised.\nThe current UI remains a disposable demo; product Vue 3 and Flutter localization are future\nwork. PR checks and review evidence are recorded in the pull request; no main deployment is\npart of this unaccepted feature branch.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0023_kitchen_ingredient_catalogue_validation_md {}

#[doc = "# Feature specifications\n\nEach stable NNNN-slug folder contains specification.md (what/why/acceptance), adrs.md\n(decisions) and plan.md (implementation and validation). Add ux-notes.md for UI features.\nLifecycle: Draft → Ready → In progress → Done. Draft implementation tasks are intentionally\nunchecked. Must means required for the intended product, not all in the initial milestone.\nNew folders take the next free number; keep index/status changes in the same commit.\n\n| Requirement | Feature | Status | Priority | Milestone |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F01 | [Server and delivery foundation](../page_specs_0001_bootstrap_specification_md/index.html) | Done | Must | M0 |\n| F02 | [Ingredient catalogue and nutrition](../page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_specification_md/index.html) | Done | Must | M1 |\n| F03 | [Precise quantities and configurable units](../page_specs_0003_quantities_units_specification_md/index.html) | Done | Must | M1 |\n| F04 | [Recipe authoring and scaling](../page_specs_0004_recipe_authoring_specification_md/index.html) | Done | Must | M1 |\n| F05 | [Recipe sharing and collections](../page_specs_0005_sharing_collections_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Must | M2 |\n| F06 | [Shopping lists and recipe provenance](../page_specs_0006_shopping_list_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Must | M2 |\n| F07 | [Preferred shops and learned shopping order](../page_specs_0007_shops_order_learning_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Should | M2 |\n| F08 | [Barcode scanning and product matching](../page_specs_0008_barcode_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Could | M3 |\n| F09 | [Household members and dietary constraints](../page_specs_0009_household_profiles_specification_md/index.html) | Done | Must | M1 |\n| F10 | [Family meal planning and calendar attendance](../page_specs_0010_meal_planning_specification_md/index.html) | Done | Must | M2 |\n| F11 | [Cooking history and online preference learning](../page_specs_0011_recommendation_feedback_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Should | M2 |\n| F12 | [Guided cooking and preset timers](../page_specs_0012_guided_cooking_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Must | M2 |\n| F13 | [Multi-day bread, rolls and pizza scheduling](../page_specs_0013_bread_schedules_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Should | M3 |\n| F14 | [Brewing and fermentation workflows](../page_specs_0014_brewing_fermentation_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Could | M4 |\n| F15 | [Inventory and shopping offers](../page_specs_0015_inventory_offers_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Should | M3 |\n| F16 | [Customer-operated recipe link import](../page_specs_0016_recipe_import_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Should | M3 |\n| F17 | [MCP recipe tools](../page_specs_0017_mcp_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Should | M3 |\n| F18 | [Storage adapters, Nextcloud `ExApp` and Flutter](../page_specs_0018_storage_deployment_specification_md/index.html) | In progress | Must | M1 |\n| F19 | [Hosted plans, paid app and recipe marketplace](../page_specs_0019_commercial_service_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Could | M4 |\n| F20 | [Federated recipe and meal-plan exchange](../page_specs_0020_federation_specification_md/index.html) | Draft | Could | M5 |\n| F21 | [Internationalization and localized content](../page_specs_0021_internationalization_specification_md/index.html) | In progress | Must | M1 |\n| F22 | [Vue 3 product web clients](../page_specs_0022_product_web_clients_specification_md/index.html) | In progress | Must | M1 |\n| F23 | [English-base kitchen ingredient catalogue](../page_specs_0023_kitchen_ingredient_catalogue_specification_md/index.html) | Done | Must | M1 |\n"]
